  "body": "## What changed\nThe scallop verifier's flank reach grows from `band + 3·tol` to `max(2r, band + 3·tol)` (`ridge::reach`). It now reads a cusp at any stepover up to the ball diameter, which is the generator's own ceiling (#37 `scallop_ceiling`). Before, it stopped at 4·tol past the ball. In #37 a plain widening convicted crowns, corners and box walls as scallop. Three cusp-geometry rules in the new `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/ridge_scan.rs` keep those false cusps out:\n1. **Nearest feet only.** Only segments within `max(cell, 3·tol)` of the nearest distance count. A cusp stands equally far from both passes.\n2. **One foot per pass.** Segments group into passes (joined runs, merged by closed iso-Z ring). Each pass counts once, at its nearest point. A free end gives no side.\n3. **Both feet in contact** (`Access::touches`). A pass riding air or skimming stock flanks nothing.\n\nThe M13.8 `Flank` struct is retired. The ridge pass moved out of `scan.rs` (431 → 359 lines) into `ridge_scan.rs` (276 lines, with a provenance header). The full decision record is in `docs/decisions/212-scallop-reach.md`.\n\n## Readings\n- Flat raster at s=4 on an r3 ball: scallop 0 before (unread), **0.606** now (the analytic cusp).\n- All 88 finish3d release-lane verdict fixtures stay clean. `morphed_spiral_dome_bites_nothing` goes from 0.1321 to 0. Flow 15/15.\n- **One existing heavy-lane assertion changed:** `verify::envelope_verdict_follows_the_stated_tol` (app, `--ignored`). Its tight half (tol 0.01 on cone rings laddered for tol 0.1) used to expect silence. It now expects exactly one **non-blocking** `Scallop` note, for the rings' real ~0.085 mm cusp. That is over the 0.01 budget and under the 0.1 the rings were laddered to. The envelope (gouge/rest) half is unchanged.\n\nNothing generated or posted changes. Only the verifier's notes change, and the Scallop note stays non-blocking.\n\n## Pinning tests\n`crates/sim/tests/ridge_reach.rs`:\n- `a_flat_raster_past_the_near_reach_is_judged_at_its_cusp`\n- `the_wider_flank_never_softens_the_old_reading`\n- `a_crown_above_the_top_lap_stays_rest_not_scallop`\n- `a_wall_top_edge_the_rings_run_beside_stays_rest_not_scallop`\n- `a_pass_clear_of_the_part_flanks_nothing`\n\n## Gate\n- Quick gate on the merge with upstream/main (51b80a5): sim suites green; app suites green except the known `probe_op::every_older_kind_keeps_its_stored_id_and_digest_tag` (#344, fixed by #345).\n- Worker runs: sim release with `--ignored` green, app release heavy lanes green, motion green (apart from the known `swarf_pose_continuity`, #351).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\nChangelog: The scallop check now reads cusps from spacings up to the ball diameter (it used to stop at 4·tol past the ball) and no longer reports false cusps at crowns, corners or air passes (#212)\n\nFixes #212\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
